# Excludes files from the static-assets Worker upload (wrangler.jsonc's
# assets.directory is the whole repo root, since index.html/player.html live
# there with no build step). Without this, wrangler scans .git's internal
# object store too - which has hit Cloudflare's 25MiB per-asset limit on old
# large blobs from before media moved to R2.
.git
worker
.wrangler
node_modules
# macOS Finder metadata, regenerated constantly in any folder browsed in
# Finder - harmless as an asset but has no reason to ever be part of the
# deployed site (see 1df28a9, where a misfired `wrangler deploy` from the
# wrong directory swept a couple of these into a deploy).
.DS_Store
# Claude Code's own local session/tool state (e.g. scheduled_tasks.lock) -
# same class of mistake as .DS_Store above, hit again the same way (a
# `wrangler deploy` run from worker/ that still resolved the repo-root
# config instead of worker/wrangler.toml - see that file's own README for
# why `--config wrangler.toml` should be passed explicitly whenever unsure).
.claude
